# dinomem git-autosnapshot — attributes
#
# ── NO git-lfs RULES HERE ANY MORE (2026-10-08) ─────────────────────────────
#
# This file USED to declare ~28 binary globs as LFS-tracked (*.mp4 *.mov *.zip
# *.tar.gz *.png *.jpg *.pdf *.psd *.woff2 ...). That single decision turned an
# auto-CHANGELOG into an accidental auto-BACKUP, and it is the whole reason this
# file is now nearly empty.
#
# HOW IT MISFIRED: auto-commit.sh has a size guard (AUTOSNAP_MAX_MB, default 10)
# so a stray dump can never bloat the snapshot store. But LFS-tracked paths were
# deliberately EXEMPTED from that guard, on the reasoning that "LFS stores their
# bytes outside history". Outside *history* — but still on disk, inside
# .dinomem-snap.git/lfs/objects. So the guard let every media file through and
# LFS kept a byte-exact second copy of it, forever.
#
# MEASURED on workspace-analyst (2026-10-08):
#   .dinomem-snap.git = 11.33 GB, of which lfs/objects = 11 GB (473 objects,
#   largest ~0.59 GB each) — 60% of the entire workspace backup.
# VERIFIED as duplicates, not assumed: an LFS object's FILENAME IS the sha256 of
# its contents, so the match is exact:
#   work/hype_video/hype_conviction_documented.mp4 -> present in lfs/objects
#   work/hype_video/archive_v5/master_v5.mp4       -> present in lfs/objects
# Both already live in the workspace, so the store was pure duplication.
# Across all 19 dinomem workspaces that is ~15.6 GB of duplicated media.
#
# THE CORRECTED PRINCIPLE (owner, 2026-10-08): "it shld be auto changelog only,
# not just for memory but for the whole workspace / no backup, no media, etc".
# A changelog needs to answer "what text changed, and let me undo it". A binary
# has no meaningful diff and no meaningful undo — you either keep the bytes or
# you do not, and keeping them is a BACKUP's job. backup.py already does that
# (and now excludes this store outright).
#
# So media is IGNORED, not tracked: the globs that used to be listed here have
# moved into gitignore.snippet. Ignoring also makes the size guard total —
# nothing can be exempted from it any more, which is what let this happen.
#
# DO NOT re-add `filter=lfs` lines here. If a binary genuinely must be
# versioned, version it in a real project repo, not in the snapshot store.

# Treat the memory/notes corpus as text so diffs stay readable and line-based.
*.md       text
*.txt      text
*.json     text
*.jsonl    text
*.yaml     text
*.yml      text
*.py       text
*.sh       text
*.ts       text
*.tsx      text
*.csv      text

# Never try to diff these; they are ignored (see gitignore.snippet) but if one is
# ever force-added, keep git from mangling or inlining it.
*.sqlite   binary
*.db       binary
*.parquet  binary
